  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer four unique one-word choices. Exactly one is the irregular past that matches the stem verb.",
      "Every stem needs a time clue (yesterday or last night) and the base form of one set-1 verb.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are far: overregularized -ed, present, and -ing of the same verb.",
      "Tier 2 may add a participle that needs have or has, such as gone, done, or given.",
      "Tier 3 uses near misses: a participle or a different set-1 past (got for give, drew for write).",
      "Never write two forms that could both complete the stem. Never invent a second past for the same verb.",
      "Keep choices in the kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands."
    ]
  },
